Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790009999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["30 of the last 33 bars are a two-sided 2357.18-2700 range with heavy overlap; the 2771 spike high made 30 bars ago is still the window high, so trend continuation is not confirmed.", "Bar 89 closed below the midpoint of its 445.69 range (buy climax), and the 2609.02-2700 area has now rejected upside probes three times (bar 113 close 2514.07 area, bar 110 high 2680 closed 2514.72, bar 118 high 2700 closed 2632.98 in the lower third of its range).", "The 120-bar window contains a full 36% bear leg (2116.86 to 1368.42) in its first 14 bars, so the window is not a single clean bull trend and the bear-trend context is only 100 bars old.", "No bar closes above 2700 yet: bar 118 leaves an upper tail and bar 119 is an inside bar, so the current push is still a boundary test, and repeated boundary tests in a range often resolve either way."], "evidence_for": ["Swing progression since the 1368.42 low is higher lows (1512.91 bar 33, 1512.91 -> 2357.18/2358.62 bars 101/114) and higher highs (1845.09, 1954.36, 1974.46, 2771), which is a bull sequence at the window level.", "The bar 87-89 spike closed far above the 24-bar 1821.49-1974.46 range and the following 30 bars never traded back below 2293.80 (bar 87 high), so the breakout was accepted rather than reversed: the range/base is left behind.", "The window's three highest closes are the last three bars (2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90), and bar 119 closes near the top of its range at 2642.90, showing buyers still pressing at the range top at the decision time.", "Lows inside the post-spike range rise after bar 101 (2374.01, 2411.04, 2413.82, 2436.87, 2568.16), a mild upward tilt consistent with a bull flag rather than a topping structure."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Bars 0-13 are a bear leg: window opens 2116.86, high 2139.34 (bar 1), low 1368.42 (bar 13), about -36% from the high.", "Bar 13 (open 1581.32, high 1599.27, low 1368.42, close 1568.55) closes 200.13 above its low, near the top of its 230.85 range: the leg ends in a climactic reversal bar rather than a trend-continuation close.", "After 1368.42 the market rallies to 1845.09 (bar 22 high) and then pulls back to 1512.91 (bar 33 low), a higher low; the subsequent leg reaches 1954.36 (bar 59 high) and 1974.46 (bar 64 high).", "Bars 63-86 are a 24-bar range between 1974.46 (bar 64 high) and 1821.49 (bar 71 low); bar 63 prints 1959.37, just above bar 59's 1954.36, and bar 64 immediately reverses to close 1891.41 near its low (failed breakout/upthrust).", "Bar 87 opens 1916.51 inside that range and closes 2252.16 (high 2293.80, low 1905.63), a +17.5% close-to-close bull bar; bar 88 closes 2326.32 and bar 89 reaches 2771.", "Bar 89 (open 2326.31, high 2771, low 2325.31, close 2515.30) closes below the midpoint 2548.16 of its 445.69 range: a long upper tail, and the 2771 high has not been exceeded in the following 30 bars.", "Bars 90-119 trade between 2357.18 (bar 101 low) and 2700 (bar 118 high) with heavy overlap and never return below 2293.80 (bar 87 high): the breakout zone 1821.49-1974.46 is left behind.", "Upside probes at 2680 (bar 110 high, close 2514.72) and 2700 (bar 118 high, close 2632.98, i.e. the lower third of its 2604.75-2700 range) both closed back inside the 30-bar range.", "Bar 114 sells to 2358.62 and closes 2397.10; the next five closes rise: 2416.57, 2446.22, 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90. Those last three are the three highest closes of the whole 120-bar window (next highest is 2515.30 on bar 89).", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is an inside bar versus bar 118 and closes 57.10 below the 2700 high, near the top of its own range."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear leg of the window ending in a climactic bar: 2116.86 open, high 2139.34 (bar 1), low 1368.42 (bar 13). Bar 13 is a bear bar closing 200.13 above its low in the upper part of its range, the exhaustion bar of the leg.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779580800000, "upper_boundary": "2139.34"}, {"description": "Mid-window trading range, 24 bars (63-86) confined between 1974.46 (bar 64 high) and 1821.49 (bar 71 low), width 152.97 (about 8%). Bar 63 marginally exceeds the prior swing high 1954.36 and bar 64 reverses to close 1891.41 near its low: a failed breakout above the prior high.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1821.49", "start_time_ms": 1785024000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the 24-bar range: bar 87 opens 1916.51 inside the range and closes 2252.16 (high 2293.80, low 1905.63); bars 88 (close 2326.32) and 89 (open 2326.31, high 2771, close 2515.30) extend it. Bar 89 closes below the midpoint of its 445.69 range (long upper tail), so the third bar is climactic.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Post-spike trading range, 30 bars (90-119): overlapping two-sided trade between 2357.18 (bar 101 low) and 2700 (bar 118 high), never returning below 2293.80 (bar 87 high). Spike highs at 2680 (bar 110) and 2700 (bar 118) were both sold back into the range; lows after bar 101 rise from 2374.01 (bar 102) to 2568.16 (bar 119) with one near-retest at 2358.62 (bar 114).", "end_time_ms": 1789948799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Recent bull leg off bar 114's low 2358.62: five rising closes 2416.57, 2446.22, 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, the highest closes of the window. Bar 117 closes 2612.02 near its 2643.52 high; bar 119 is an inside bar versus bar 118 and closes 2642.90, 57.10 under the 2700 range top. Still a leg inside the 30-bar range, not an accepted breakout.", "end_time_ms": 1789948799999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789430400000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["A daily close above 2700 (bar 118 high) with a further bull close would mark acceptance of an upside breakout from the 30-bar range and support continued bull-trend/channel behaviour.", "A bear close below 2568.16 (bar 119 low) followed by a break of 2357.18 (bar 101 low) would break the 30-bar range low and shift the read toward a lower high under 2771 and a range-down resolution.", "Continuation of overlapping bars contained inside 2436.87 (bar 117 low) and 2700 keeps the phase 'range' and keeps always-in relevance low.", "A move back below 2293.80 (bar 87 high, the top of the breakout bar's range) would undercut breakout acceptance and move the classification toward transition-unclear."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789991999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Bar 120 closed 2723.15, only about a third of the way up its 2658.06-2850 range; the 126.85 upper tail means sellers were active at the high and the breakout has no follow-through bar yet.", "The window's comparable wide bull spike (bar 61: 2457.12 to 2555.52, high 2680, range 235.81) was followed by 25 bars inside 2358.62-2609.02 and a full retrace to 2358.62; the bar-13 spike was likewise reversed by bar 19. Repeated bull spikes have been faded in this window.", "The advance from 2358.62 is overlapping and channel-like: a 2700 to 2568.16 (-4.9%) seven-bar pullback (bars 108-114), and earlier a 2680 to 2358.62 (-12.0%) decline, i.e., deep two-sided swings rather than one-way trending.", "Most of the 120-bar window traded between 2357.18 and 2700, so the broader context is a wide range and 2850 sits at/just beyond its upper extreme."], "evidence_for": ["Higher highs and higher lows since the 2358.62 low (bar 86): highs 2585.5, 2643.52, 2700, 2850 against lows 2436.87, 2568.16, 2658.06.", "Bar 120 closed 2723.15, above the 12-bar range top 2700 and above every prior high in the window, on a 191.94-point range bar with a 64.34-point bull body.", "The double bottom 2357.18 (bar 6) / 2358.62 (bar 86) held and was followed by a rally of roughly 21% into 2850.", "Recent closes step higher with little overlap (2577.88, 2611.0, 2631.93, 2642.9, 2664.73) before the breakout bar."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars, 1788264000000-178999199199999; first close 2451.89, last close 2723.15; window low 2357.18 (bar 6), window high 2850 (bar 120).", "Bars 1-60 were two-sided inside 2357.18-2537.57: bar 13 spiked 2407.48 to 2506.79 (high 2509.15), bar 19 reversed 2523.22 to 2450.96 (low 2436.73), and bars 20-60 kept overlapping, with a bull-trap tail high of 2680 already seen at bar 61.", "Bar 61 (1789128000000) is the widest bar of the window: 2457.12 to 2555.52, high 2680, low 2444.19, range 235.81 with a 124.48 upper tail; the following 25 bars stayed inside 2358.62-2609.02.", "Bars 82-86 sold off to 2358.62 (bar 86 low), a near-retest of the window low 2357.18; the low held and bars 87-103 rallied 2358.62 to 2585.5 on mostly rising closes (bar 103: 2507.15 to 2578.6).", "Bars 104-114 pulled back in overlapping bars to 2568.16 (bar 114 low), holding above the bar-103 low 2495.82; bars 115-119 then rallied 2611.0 to 2658.81 and tagged 2700 (bar 118 high).", "Bar 120 opened 2658.81, ran to 2850 and closed 2723.15 (+64.34); its 191.94 range is the second widest of the window, but the close sits in the lower third of that range, leaving a 126.85 upper tail above the prior range top 2700 and the window high 2680.", "Six of the last eight closes were higher (bars 114-120: 2577.88, 2611.0, 2631.93, 2642.9, 2664.73, 2723.15)."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "First-half two-sided balance inside 2357.18-2537.57; the bar-13 bull spike was fully reversed by bar 19, and bars 20-60 kept overlapping with a spike low of 2411.04 at bar 55.", "end_time_ms": 1789127999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1788264000000, "upper_boundary": "2537.57"}, {"description": "Mid-window balance after the bar-61 spike (2457.12 to 2555.52, high 2680, upper tail 124.48); bodies stayed roughly 2469-2609 and the top was tagged again at 2609.02 on bar 81 (close 2514.07) before bars 82-86 fell to 2358.62.", "end_time_ms": 1789502399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789128000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 2358.62 low with higher highs 2585.5 (bar 103), 2643.52 (bar 104), 2700 (bars 108 and 118) and 2850 (bar 120) against higher lows 2436.87 (bar 100), 2568.16 (bar 114) and 2658.06 (bar 120); overlapping bars and a 131.84-point pullback (2700 to 2568.16, bars 108-114) keep it channel-like rather than a clean spike.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789502400000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Twelve-bar balance 2568.16-2700 (bars 108-119) from which the final bar broke; both bar 108 and bar 118 printed 2700 highs.", "end_time_ms": 1789977599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2568.16", "start_time_ms": 1789804800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "One-bar breakout attempt: bar 120 (2658.81 to 2723.15) closed above the 2700 range top and above the prior window high 2680, but gave back 126.85 of its 191.94 range, so acceptance above the range is not yet shown.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2658.06", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Follow-through: a further bull bar closing above 2723.15 and holding above 2750 would confirm the breakout and support continuation of the breakout-spike phase.", "Failure: two consecutive closes back below 2700 would recast bar 120 as a failed breakout and return the structure to the 2568.16-2700 range.", "Exhaustion: a close back below the bar-120 low 2658.06 would flag bar 120 as a climactic bar and push the phase toward transition.", "Trend break: a close below 2568.16 would break the higher-low sequence (2436.87, 2568.16, 2658.06) and question the bull-trend classification.", "Continued overlapping bars inside 2658.06-2723.15 without a new high would keep the read channel/range rather than spike."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "stale"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2384.88", "close_time_ms": 1789581599999, "high": "2392.25", "low": "2370.54", "open": "2391.1", "open_time_ms": 1789578000000, "volume": "2783910.164"}, {"close": "2394.67", "close_time_ms": 1789585199999, "high": "2419.22", "low": "2377.61", "open": "2384.88", "open_time_ms": 1789581600000, "volume": "3152893.004"}, {"close": "2407.99", "close_time_ms": 1789588799999, "high": "2412.49", "low": "2378.84", "open": "2391.89", "open_time_ms": 1789585200000, "volume": "2055736.612"}, {"close": "2410.09", "close_time_ms": 1789592399999, "high": "2416.72", "low": "2404.55", "open": "2407.91", "open_time_ms": 1789588800000, "volume": "2360830.123"}, {"close": "2404.17", "close_time_ms": 1789595999999, "high": "2411.77", "low": "2400.28", "open": "2410.13", "open_time_ms": 1789592400000, "volume": "1949272.699"}, {"close": "2392.19", "close_time_ms": 1789599599999, "high": "2404.61", "low": "2389.13", "open": "2404.18", "open_time_ms": 1789596000000, "volume": "2068552.579"